libass: assemble x86 code for QNX as ELF.

configure picks the nasm object format from the host OS and does not list
QNX, which on x86 is ELF with the SysV ABI's 16-byte stack alignment like the
systems already listed. configure is regenerated by the recipe.

Upstream-Status: Pending

diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index c0977c5..f5d34a4 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -300,7 +300,10 @@ AS_IF([test "x$enable_asm" != xno], [
                             ASFLAGS="$ASFLAGS -DPREFIX"
                         ])
                     ],
-                    [linux*|solaris*|haiku*|gnu*], [
+                    [linux*|solaris*|haiku*|gnu*|nto-qnx*|nto*|qnx*], [
+                        dnl QNX on x86 is ELF with the SysV ABI's 16-byte stack
+                        dnl alignment, exactly like the platforms above -- the
+                        dnl list simply predates anyone building libass for it.
                         ASFLAGS="$ASFLAGS -f elf$BITTYPE -DSTACK_ALIGNMENT=16"
                     ],
                     [dragonfly*|*bsd*], [
